  "body": "Per the current spec (also after #1404 tweaks it), I believe the following code is specced to work:\n\n``` js\nwindow.customElements.define(\"a-valid-custom-element-name\", HTMLButtonElement);\n```\n\nThis seems bad, right? I guess maaaybe it could be made to work? But it probably shouldn't.\n\nEven this works:\n\n``` js\nwindow.customElements.define(\"another-valid-custom-element-name\", SharedWorker);\n```\n\nalthough you won't be able to successfully create any such elements, as the brand check after attempting to do so will fail.\n\nIn spec-ese, we can easily disallow these by saying \"If _constructor_ is a platform object interface, throw a TypeError\". Is that something that is easy to implement? Should I put it in the spec?\n\n@dominiccooney @kojiishi @rniwa @bzbarsky \n",
